Shak., Lear, iv. 1. 7.—'''2.''' Not real; not having substance; imaginary; illusive: as, ''unsubstantial'' forms. ''Rowe'', Lady Jane Grey, iv.—'''3.''' Not having good substance; not strong or stout: as, an ''unsubstantial'' building; ''unsubstantial'' cloth.—'''4.''' Not giving substance or strength; weak; not strengthening or invigorating.
